{"path":"/documentation/modeling/vllm/serve/http","section":"documentation","title":"http","description":"Documentation for the nnsight Python library","toc":[{"id":"nnsight.modeling.vllm.serve.http","label":"http","depth":2},{"id":"nnsight.modeling.vllm.serve.http.CONNECT_TIMEOUT","label":"CONNECT_TIMEOUT\n\n\n  \n      module-attribute","depth":3},{"id":"nnsight.modeling.vllm.serve.http.READ_TIMEOUT","label":"READ_TIMEOUT\n\n\n  \n      module-attribute","depth":3},{"id":"nnsight.modeling.vllm.serve.http.timeout","label":"timeout","depth":3},{"id":"nnsight.modeling.vllm.serve.http.headers","label":"headers","depth":3},{"id":"nnsight.modeling.vllm.serve.http.check","label":"check","depth":3}],"segments":[{"type":"html","html":"<h2 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.serve.http\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-module\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-module-name\">http</span>\n\n\n</h2>"},{"type":"html","html":"<p>What both halves of the serve client put on the wire.</p>\n<p>A trace and an installed block reach a server the same way — the same headers,\nthe same timeouts, the same reading of a non-200 — but from two unrelated places:\n<a title=\"            LocalServeBackend\" href=\"/documentation/modeling/vllm/serve/backend#nnsight.modeling.vllm.serve.backend.LocalServeBackend\"><code>LocalServeBackend</code></a> sends\nthe trace, and\n<a title=\"            ServeRegistration\" href=\"/documentation/modeling/vllm/registration#nnsight.modeling.vllm.registration.ServeRegistration\"><code>ServeRegistration</code></a> sends\nthe block. Keeping the wire details here is what stops the two from drifting; the\nerror message in particular is one a user reads, and two copies of it would\ndiverge on the first edit.</p>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h3 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.serve.http.CONNECT_TIMEOUT\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-attribute\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-attribute-name\">CONNECT_TIMEOUT</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-module-attribute\"><code>module-attribute</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h3>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"CONNECT_TIMEOUT: float = 10.0"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h3 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.serve.http.READ_TIMEOUT\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-attribute\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-attribute-name\">READ_TIMEOUT</span>\n\n\n  <span class=\"doc-labels\">\n      <small class=\"doc-label doc-label-module-attribute\"><code>module-attribute</code></small>\n  </span>\n\n</h3>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"READ_TIMEOUT: float = 600.0"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h3 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.serve.http.timeout\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-function\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">timeout</span>\n\n\n</h3>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"timeout() -> Any"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h3 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.serve.http.headers\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-function\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">headers</span>\n\n\n</h3>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"headers(api_key: Optional[str] = None, compress: bool = False) -> dict"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n        <p>The headers every nnsight-serve request carries.</p>\n\n\n    </div>"},{"type":"html","html":"<h3 id=\"nnsight.modeling.vllm.serve.http.check\" class=\"doc-heading\">\n<code class=\"doc-symbol doc-symbol-heading doc-symbol-function\"></code>            <span class=\"doc-object-name doc-function-name\">check</span>\n\n\n</h3>"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","code":"check(response: Any) -> None"},{"type":"html","html":"<div class=\"doc-contents\">\n\n        <p>Raise the server's own explanation of a non-200, as a <code>ConnectionError</code>.</p>\n<p>A transport or service failure, as distinct from an error <em>inside</em> the trace —\nthat one comes back in the body as a deferred error and is re-raised at the\nclient with its real type.</p>\n\n\n    </div>"}]}